# Xana — environment template.
#
# Copy this to `.env` and fill in a key. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not,
# and it must never contain a real key.
#
#   cp .env.example .env      # then edit .env
#
# `npm run dev` watches this file and reloads it, so a change takes effect on
# the next request — no restart.
#
# TWO THINGS WORTH KNOWING BEFORE YOU PASTE ANYTHING
#
# 1. A key here does NOT switch the model on. Xana needs the key AND the
#    "use the model" toggle in Settings, because someone who has OPENAI_API_KEY
#    exported for another tool has not thereby agreed to Xana spending it.
#    Paste the key, then open Settings → Model & key and switch it on.
#
# 2. For voice, you do not need a key at all — see the audio section at the
#    bottom. Xana speaks and listens through your own browser.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# The model that writes her replies
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# DeepSeek. Cheap, strong at reasoning, OpenAI-compatible.
# The variable name selects the endpoint, so you do not also set a base URL:
# `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` implies https://api.deepseek.com/v1 and deepseek-chat.
#
# Get one at https://platform.deepseek.com/api_keys
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# Any one of these works the same way — the name picks the endpoint.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# TOGETHER_API_KEY=

# A generic key, for an endpoint none of the names above describe (Ollama,
# llama.cpp, a company gateway). It outranks a provider-branded variable, and
# it does NOT imply an endpoint — pair it with XANA_LLM_BASE_URL.
# XANA_LLM_API_KEY=

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Overrides, only if you need them
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Force a different endpoint. A base URL set here is used as-is; this is the
# "point Xana at my own llama.cpp" switch.
# XANA_LLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1

# Force a different model on that endpoint, e.g. deepseek-reasoner.
# XANA_LLM_MODEL=deepseek-chat

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the data lives
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Moves BOTH the database and the settings file. Useful for a container, a
# mounted volume, or a scratch run that must not touch your real life.
# XANA_DATA_DIR=

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audio: speaking and listening
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# No key is needed, and no audio ever reaches the model.
#
# SPEAKING (text to speech) happens in your browser, through the voices Windows
# and your browser already have installed. Switch it on in Settings → Voice,
# and pick a voice. `speakReplies` is stored in data/settings.json, not here.
#
# LISTENING (speech to text) is the browser's SpeechRecognition API, which the
# mic button beside the input uses. It is shown only in a browser that has the
# API — Edge and Chrome do.
#
# Two ways it can run, and the difference matters for privacy:
#
#   on-device  the audio never leaves the machine. Requires Edge Dev/Canary
#              150.0.4076+ with `edge://flags` → "Speech Recognition with
#              on-device model" set to Enabled. Xana detects it and uses it,
#              and falls back to it automatically if the cloud path fails.
#
#   cloud      the browser sends the audio to its own speech service. Nothing
#              is sent to Xana or to DeepSeek, and no key is involved — but it
#              does leave the machine, and it needs a working connection.
#
# If a server-side transcription API is ever wanted — for an audio file rather
# than the microphone — the providers below all offer one. None of them is used
# by Xana today; they are listed because this is where such a key would go.
#
#   Groq       https://console.groq.com/keys          free tier, whisper-large-v3
#   OpenAI     https://platform.openai.com/api-keys   gpt-4o-mini-transcribe
#   (DeepSeek has no audio model — see the README)
#
# GROQ_API_KEY=
